  "answer_markdown": "Yes, when you start a remote coding session from a Slack thread with **Vibe Code Web**, the agent can open a **merge request (pull request)** for you to review, provided the task is scoped and actionable within the thread context [2][3][5].\n\n### How it works:\n1. The agent reads the Slack thread context and maps it to a **Vibe Code Web project** and **GitHub repository** [3].\n2. It works in an **isolated cloud sandbox** and creates a **GitHub branch** with the proposed changes [3][5].\n3. If the changes are appropriate, it **opens a pull request** for review in GitHub [2][3][5].\n\n### Example prompt to trigger this:\n```text\n@Vibe investigate the issue described in this thread and open a PR if there is a clear fix.\n```\n\n### Key requirements:\n- The Slack thread must contain **enough context** (e.g., repository, bug description, constraints) [2].\n- The task should be **small and scoped** (e.g., fixing a failing test, implementing an agreed change) [2][4].\n- The agent **does not merge the PR automatically**—you must review and approve it in GitHub [3][5].",
