  "answer_markdown": "Vibe requires explicit approval for sensitive actions across its tools. Here’s how it works:\n\n### **Approval Process for Sensitive Actions**\n\n1. **Trigger for Approval**: Before performing actions like sending emails, posting messages, modifying files, or deleting data, Vibe **pauses and asks for approval** [1][2][5][6].\n\n2. **Approval Options**: You have three choices:\n   - **Continue**: Approve the specific action only (Vibe will ask again next time) [1].\n   - **Always allow**: Pre-authorize the function for the current session (no further prompts) [1].\n   - **Decline**: Cancel the action (Vibe may skip the step or ask for alternatives) [1].\n\n3. **Where Approvals Appear**:\n   - **Vibe Work (CLI/Web)**: Approval prompts appear inline in the chat, with keyboard shortcuts like `Enter` (approve) or `N` (reject) [7].\n   - **VS Code Extension**: Approvals appear in the Mistral Vibe side panel, with shortcuts like `Mod+Y` (approve) or `Mod+Alt+N` (reject) [7].\n   - **Vibe Code Web**: Approvals appear in the browser UI, tied to GitHub repository permissions [7].\n\n4. **Review Before Approving**: Always verify details like recipients, content, or file changes before approving [1][3][7].\n\n### **Pre-Authorization**\nYou can pre-authorize specific functions per Connector (e.g., always allow email sending) via [Per-function Connector permissions](https://docs.mistral.ai/vibe/work/safety-and-approvals#connector-functions) [2].\n\n### **Interrupting Actions**\nUse the **stop button (black square)** to interrupt a running action, though this may not work if the action has already reached the external system [1][5].\n\n---",
