  "answer_markdown": "Yes, the model `codestral-2508` supports **Fill-in-the-Middle (FIM)** for code completion tasks. This is explicitly confirmed in the [model capability matrix](https://docs.mistral.ai/models), where `codestral-2508` is listed alongside `codestral-2501` as supporting FIM [1].

To use FIM with this model, you can structure your request as follows (example from the [FIM API documentation](https://docs.mistral.ai/api/endpoint/fim#operation-fim_completion_v1_fim_completions_post)):

```json
{
  "model": "codestral-2508",
  "prompt": "def calculate_factorial(n):\n    if n <= 1:\n        return 1\n    return n * calculate_factorial(",
  "suffix": ")",
  "max_tokens": 50
}
```

In this example, the model will generate the missing part between the `prompt` and `suffix` (e.g., completing the recursive call).

For further details on the FIM API, refer to the [official documentation](https://docs.mistral.ai/api/endpoint/fim) [2].",
